Great episode by @ajambrosino. Taste is so important but also way more than just pretty UI design.

@ajambrosino, who leads the team behind the Codex desktop app at @OpenAI, discusses how the app's usage has increased sixfold since February, reaching over 5 million weekly active users, with nearly all OpenAI employees using it regularly. He aims to build the best desktop app ever, and the conversation covers topics like how product managers at OpenAI operate, why AI struggles with design, the timing of the app’s release, and what 'taste' really means as a professional skill. He also shares how he uses Codex in his workflows and his vision for integrating Codex with ChatGPT.

The linked video is from Lenny's Podcast.

